Rationale: The claim states that Aiko, Princess Toshi is the only child of the Japanese princess born in 1963. The evidence confirms that Aiko is the only child of Empress Masako, who was born on 9 December 1963. However, the claim is contradicted because it implies that Empress Masako is the only Japanese princess born in 1963, but there is no evidence to support this exclusivity. Additionally, the claim is structured to imply that the Japanese princess born in 1963 is the sole parent of Aiko, which is not explicitly confirmed by the evidence. Reliable evidence contradicts the completeness of the claim.
